Z||000004||Fformula88||10-26-2001||02:15 PM||||I say he is worthy of owning a Fiero, but not any Fiero.  It would have to be one that needed a lot of TLC to get going again, and then a lot more work to make it fast.  that way, by the time he was done with the project he would know the car well and appreciate it for what it is.<P>A very tired 84 2m4 would be perfect.  Finish gone on the paint, headlight motors shot, the base steel wheels with the center caps, no luggage rack (well, maybe) and at least 125k miles on it!<P>Even if he doesn't appreciate it when he's done, at least there will be one more rehabilitated Fiero!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Blondie88||10-26-2001||07:48 PM||||Come on, even cocky jerks need a break sometimes.  Sure, he's not tough enough to actually come in here and admits he's wrong, but whoever hasn't acted like that should cast the first stone!! Okay, put the stones down.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> I of course haven't been offended by him, so I guess you guys have your own reasons. If he likes fieros, that's all that should matter right??  Now, if he ever comes in again bashing fieros, then you should kick his narcicistic butt back to his mustang so he can live a pathetic mass- produced life!  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||kempo||10-26-2001||08:10 PM||||I think of it this way.  He has appologized to us for things that he felt he did wrong.  He hasn't given up on trying to be included in this forum, and that should make a statement all it's own.  He's trying to get along with us, so perhaps we should all give him a second chance, or whathaveyou.  jm$.02<P>-Kemp||||reg||1
Z||000007||Return of Fiero||10-27-2001||04:21 PM||||to be honest, i think he is kind of amusing. every time ive seem him boast a Mustang, I thought of when i was 17, with my Fiero in Manchester. on the stip there we would race 'em, and i would love to be part. i had S___ Stain owners coming up, and reving the engine, then ask what i had under the hood. "four cylinder" i would reply, and they would laugh and say ill wait on the other side for you. when the light changed, they would punch it, and i would hessitate, rev it up, release the clutch, and in a cloud of smoke, pas the Mustang like they were on the brakes. ANY Mustang can win out on ANY Fiero? humph, good laugh to think back, and Blackstain, umn stang let me do just that.its amazing what happes to a fire when you drop a Lotus 4 cyl in it. lmao<BR>BTW untill he can admit he was wrong, he doesnt deserve a Fiero. We are a breed, and have our own race to comform to, he doesnt fit. there is the drivers, who love the Fiero, but just use it to cruise, and go to work. There is the enthusiest, who wants to own, resore to original. the collector, who wants as many as he/she can handle working on and restoring. The theres the mods crew, who want to see what they can make these bad boys do. This is us, all of us. REAL Fiero drivers, the proud. we all fit one or more of the classes, but we all have one thing in common : we all love the Fiero, the Pontiac Fiero "Pride" <P>Myke<BR>ps, sorry about the Fiero patriotisim, seemed to fit. lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
